{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":482498,"name":"Aaron","username":"aaron_72","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/48db29/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-03T16:46:02.448Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eFollow-up to \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-computers-local-exec-keeps-dropping-while-mac-mini-stays-on/169848\"\u003eGrok Bot Computers / local-exec keeps dropping while Mac mini stays on\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482498-summary-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482498-summary-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSummary\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLocal-exec registration for both of my registered Macs flaps between connected and empty even though:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eboth machines stay powered on\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSettings → Computer lists both with “Execution on this computer” = Always allow\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003echat remains usable when the machines disappear from agents’ live machine lists\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis matches the known helper-process bug Colin described in that thread (cloud environment going idle → Mac helper wrongly concludes the desktop app is gone and shuts itself down). A fix was said to ship in a release after 0.29.0. I updated Grok Bot on Aarons-MBP-2 to the latest available build today and the flap is still happening.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482498-what-agents-see-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482498-what-agents-see-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat agents see\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003eListMachines\u003c/code\u003e returns \u003ccode\u003e{\"machines\": []}\u003c/code\u003e for long stretches.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMachine-targeted Shell fails with either:\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003eCommand failed to spawn: No registered machines were available when this turn started. A connected machine can be used on the next turn.\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eor, earlier, a stale machineId enum rejection while the other Mac was still listed: \u003ccode\u003eInvalid enum value. Expected '\u0026lt;other-machine-id\u0026gt;', received '\u0026lt;this-machine-id\u0026gt;'\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhen the link is briefly up, both machines appear as \u003ccode\u003econnected: true\u003c/code\u003e, then go empty again within tens of seconds to a few minutes.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482498-what-the-app-shows-at-the-same-time-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482498-what-the-app-shows-at-the-same-time-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat the app shows at the same time\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSettings → Computer lists:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAarons-Work-Mac.local — Always allow (current computer)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAarons-MBP-2 — Always allow\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo the desktop app still knows about the machines while agents’ live registration query returns empty.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482498-timeline-all-times-et-2026-09-03-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482498-timeline-all-times-et-2026-09-03-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTimeline (all times ET, 2026-09-03)\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e~10:39am — agents successfully running commands on both Macs\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e~11:31am — still working on Aarons-MBP-2\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e~11:46–11:49am — both machines go empty; every subsequent \u003ccode\u003eListMachines\u003c/code\u003e call returns \u003ccode\u003e[]\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGrok Bot restart on the work Mac: no change\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSign out / sign back in on the work Mac: no change\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRemoting into Aarons-MBP-2 via Screen Sharing (waking the GUI session): machines briefly reappeared and another agent could use MBP-2 again\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUpdated Grok Bot on Aarons-MBP-2 to latest\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e~12:33pm — both machines showed connected again\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e~30 seconds later — \u003ccode\u003eListMachines\u003c/code\u003e empty again\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482498-things-that-did-did-not-help-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482498-things-that-did-did-not-help-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThings that did / did not help\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDid \u003cstrong\u003enot\u003c/strong\u003e fix it:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRestarting Grok Bot\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSigning out and back in\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWaiting and retrying many times\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUpdating Grok Bot on Aarons-MBP-2 to the latest available build (still flaps after update)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTemporarily restored the link:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpening / focusing Grok Bot on the Mac, or waking the session via Screen Sharing\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482498-machines-are-healthy-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482498-machines-are-healthy-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMachines are healthy\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWork Mac is the machine I’m chatting from.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAarons-MBP-2 answers over Tailscale at ~5ms with 0% packet loss; SSH and VNC accept connections when the Mac is awake.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482498-possibly-related-symptoms-in-the-same-window-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482498-possibly-related-symptoms-in-the-same-window-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePossibly related symptoms in the same window\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAn agent-to-agent message was delivered to the recipient, but the recipient’s reply never arrived in the sender’s context.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eA couple of assistant replies did not visibly land in chat.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482498-ask-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482498-ask-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAsk\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIs the post-0.29.0 fix in the build I just got, or still rolling out? If it’s supposed to be in latest, this looks like a regression or an incomplete fix — happy to provide build numbers / logs if useful.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-04T08:17:42.466Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":23,"reads":6,"readers_count":5,"score":131.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":170488,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-computers-local-exec-still-flapping-after-update","display_username":"Aaron","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-computers-local-exec-keeps-dropping-while-mac-mini-stays-on/169848","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Grok Bot Computers / local-exec keeps dropping while Mac mini stays on","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136002,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-computers-local-exec-still-flapping-after-update/170488/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":482500,"name":"system","username":"system","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/system/{size}/99069_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-03T16:46:12.431Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi there!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe detected that this may be a bug report, so we’ve moved your post to the \u003cstrong\u003eBug Reports\u003c/strong\u003e category.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo help us investigate and fix this faster, could you edit your original post to include the details from the template below?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003e\nBug Report Template - Click to expand\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"9:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Editor, Tab \u0026amp; Chat (autocomplete, Composer, in-editor agent)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"10:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Terminal \u0026amp; commands\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"11:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Models, pricing \u0026amp; API keys (availability, Auto/Max, BYOK/Bedrock)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"12:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e MCP \u0026amp; tools\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"13:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Cloud Agents \u0026amp;