03e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"48:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Windows 10/11\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"49:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e MacOS\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"50:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Linux\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVersion Information\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFor Cursor IDE: Menu → About Cursor → Copy\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFor Cursor CLI: Run \u003ccode\u003eagent about\u003c/code\u003e in your terminal\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003eIDE:\nVersion: 2.xx.x\nVSCode Version: 1.105.1\nCommit: ......\n\nCLI:\nCLI Version 2026.01.17-d239e66\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFor AI issues: which model did you use?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nModel name (e.g., Sonnet 4, Tab…)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFor AI issues: add Request ID with privacy disabled\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nRequest ID: f9a7046a-279b-47e5-ab48-6e8dc12daba1\u003cbr\u003e\nFor Background Agent issues, also post the ID: bc-…\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nAdd any other context about the problem here.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"87:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Yes - Cursor is unusable\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"88:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Sometimes - I can sometimes use Cursor\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"89:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e No - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe more details you provide, the easier it is for us to reproduce and fix the issue. Thanks!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-03T16:46:12.431Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":7,"readers_count":6,"score":6.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":170488,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-computers-local-exec-still-flapping-after-update","display_username":"system","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://cursor.com/agents","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":-1,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-computers-local-exec-still-flapping-after-update/170488/2","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":482968,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-04T08:17:15.548Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report with the timeline. It matches exactly what we saw on our side.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTwo separate things overlapped here.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFirst, to answer your direct question: the helper process fix from the previous thread is indeed out. It’s in 0.30.0 and newer, so it should be on both of your Macs. What happened today is not a regression of that fix.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat hit today starting around 11:46am ET is a separate issue on our side. Because of a change in a recent release, your account briefly looked like it was in Legacy Privacy Mode, and requests from cloud computer were getting rejected. That’s why the computer list came back empty, even though in Settings both Macs were set to Always allow. This also explains a couple assistant responses that didn’t make it into the chat, and the lost agent-to-agent reply.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe shipped a server-side fix and it fully rolled out around 12:40pm ET. From that point, cloud computer has been working normally again with both Macs, so you don’t need to reinstall anything or reset anything on your side. Restarting the app or signing out and back in during that window wouldn’t have helped either. Sorry for the extra churn.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne more thing: even before today’s incident, the Mac that was still on 0.30.0 would sometimes drop out of the list and then come back on its own in about a minute. That’s most likely the \u003ccode\u003eInvalid enum value\u003c/code\u003e you saw while the other Mac was still listed. Now that both are on 0.36.0, this should happen much less often. If a Mac still disappears from \u003ccode\u003eListMachines\u003c/code\u003e for more than a couple of minutes, send the time (ET is fine) and which Mac it was, and we’ll take a look.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-04T08:17:15.548Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":6,"readers_count":5,"score":31.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":170488,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-computers-local-exec-still-flapping-after-update","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":2}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-computers-local-exec-still-flapping-after-update/170488/6","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":2}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":2,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":484692,"name":"Rob","username":"ras434","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/ras434/{size}/120070_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-06T19:50:25.082Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eResidual report on Grok Bot 0.43.0 (after app update + reboot), same family as this thread and the “Mac stays on / local-exec drops” reports.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHardware (no hostname): MacBook Pro, Apple M2 Pro, 32 GB RAM\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOS: macOS 26.6.2 (build 25G83)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot: 0.43.0\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile actively using the Mac (awake, chatting back-and-forth — no sleep gap), agents still hit brief “temporarily unreachable” / local-exec drops. One confirmed today ~1:51pm America/New_York: recovered on its own in ~1–2 minutes with no quit/relaunch. Chat stayed up the whole time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStaff asked here to report if a Mac stays missing more than a couple of minutes; ours are usually the short self-heal case, but it still interrupts mid-job on current builds while the machine is clearly in ac